cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The three-shift radical problem has no solution: an elementary obstruction"
abstract: >-
  We prove that there are no distinct positive integers x and y whose prime-divisor
  sets agree simultaneously at the shifts 0, 1 and 2. The first and third conditions
  are already contradictory: rad(x) = rad(x+2) is impossible, because x and x+2 have
  coprime odd parts. This answers the three-shift question recorded as Erdos problem
  #850 and as JSP-000703 in the negative.
message: "If you use this result, please cite the repository URL and the commit SHA you used."
